    <h2>Employee Information</h2><p>**Current Employee Count:** 501-1,000 employees (according to Seamless.AI)

**Alternative Estimate:** ~1,137 employees (according to Growjo.com)

**Key Growth Context:**
- The company doubled its staff in 2021 according to Dallas Innovates reporting
- This growth coincided with their $95M Series B funding round in December 2021
- The company has been in rapid expansion mode since then

**Important Distinction:**
ShiftSmart has over 2.2 million workers on their platform across 57 countries, but these are gig workers/contractors who use the platform for flexible work opportunities - they are not full-time employees of ShiftSmart. The actual ShiftSmart corporate employees (the people who work directly for the company building and operating the platform) appear to be in the 500-1,100 range based on the most recent available data.</p><h1>ShiftSmart Company Research Report</h1><h2>Executive Summary</h2><p>ShiftSmart is a leading workforce management platform that revolutionizes the hourly labor market by connecting flexible workers with employers through an end-to-end technology solution. Founded in 2015, the company has grown to serve over 2.2 million workers across 57 countries and has raised over $120 million in funding from top-tier investors.</p><h2>Company Overview</h2><p><strong>Founded:</strong> 2015<br><strong>Headquarters:</strong> Dallas, Texas (originally), New York operations<br><strong>Mission:</strong> "Changing The World Through Flexible Work"<br><strong>Industry:</strong> Workforce Management, Gig Economy, Labor Technology</p><p>ShiftSmart operates as a comprehensive labor management platform that enables companies to fractionalize jobs into shifts while providing hourly workers with flexible scheduling options and increased earning opportunities.</p><h2>Business Model</h2><h3>Core Services</h3><ul><li><p><strong>Workforce Sourcing:</strong> Connecting employers with qualified hourly workers</p></li><li><p><strong>Scheduling Management:</strong> Advanced scheduling tools for shift-based work</p></li><li><p><strong>Deployment &amp; Management:</strong> End-to-end workforce deployment solutions</p></li><li><p><strong>Payment Processing:</strong> Streamlined payment systems for workers</p></li><li><p><strong>Quality Review:</strong> Performance monitoring and quality assurance tools</p></li></ul><h3>Target Markets</h3><ul><li><p>Retail</p></li><li><p>Hospitality</p></li><li><p>Manufacturing</p></li><li><p>Service Industries</p></li><li><p>Government Agencies</p></li></ul><h3>Key Value Propositions</h3><p><strong>For Workers:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Flexible scheduling control</p></li><li><p>Increased earning opportunities</p></li><li><p>Access to diverse job opportunities</p></li><li><p>Digital-first experience</p></li></ul><p><strong>For Employers:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Enhanced fulfillment rates</p></li><li><p>Reduced turnover</p></li><li><p>Improved quality standards</p></li><li><p>Scalable workforce solutions</p></li><li><p>Cost-effective labor management</p></li></ul><h2>Leadership Team</h2><h3>Key Executives</h3><p><strong>Aakash Kumar - Founder &amp; CEO</strong></p><ul><li><p>Previously Cloud Business Operations and Strategy Lead at Google</p></li><li><p>Specialized in labor dynamics and managing large distributed workforces</p></li><li><p>Named Ernst &amp; Young Entrepreneur of the Year 2022 New York Award finalist</p></li><li><p>Responsible for developing ShiftSmart's "People-First" philosophy</p></li></ul><p><strong>Pavan Patel - Co-Founder &amp; CTO</strong></p><ul><li><p>Joined ShiftSmart in 2016</p></li><li><p>Leads research and development of platform technology</p></li><li><p>Previously software engineer at Simply Hired</p></li><li><p>Responsible for platform functionality and delivery</p></li></ul><p><strong>Other Leadership:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Sid Singh - SVP, Retail</p></li><li><p>Richard Zicchino - Chief Compliance Officer</p></li></ul><h2>Funding and Financial Information</h2><h3>Total Funding Raised: $120.6 Million</h3><p><strong>Series B (December 2021): $95 Million</strong></p><ul><li><p>Led by D1 Capital Partners</p></li><li><p>Participants: Imaginary Ventures, OakRidge Management Group, S12F, Spieker Partners</p></li><li><p>Additional undisclosed investors and industry executives</p></li></ul><p><strong>Previous Rounds:</strong> $25.6 Million (across multiple earlier rounds)</p><h3>Growth Metrics</h3><ul><li><p>Over 2.2 million workers (partners) on platform</p></li><li><p>Operations in 57 countries</p></li><li><p>Doubled both staff and revenue in 2021</p></li><li><p>Serves major clients including Google, Deloitte, Circle K, and Facebook</p></li></ul><h2>Market Position and Competition</h2><h3>Industry Context</h3><p>ShiftSmart operates in the $2 trillion hourly work industry in the US alone, addressing fundamental changes in the labor market accelerated by COVID-19 and evolving worker preferences for flexibility and digital-first experiences.</p><h3>Key Competitors</h3><ul><li><p><strong>Homebase:</strong> Workforce management and scheduling platform</p></li><li><p><strong>Deputy:</strong> Employee scheduling and workforce management</p></li><li><p><strong>Nowsta:</strong> Cloud-based workforce management platform</p></li><li><p>Other gig economy platforms and traditional staffing agencies</p></li></ul><h3>Competitive Advantages</h3><ul><li><p>End-to-end technology platform</p></li><li><p>Scale with 2.2M+ workers globally</p></li><li><p>Enterprise focus with major corporate clients</p></li><li><p>"People-First" philosophy</p></li></ul><p>Advanced fractionali</p><h2>Employee Information</h2><p>**Current Employee Count:** 501-1,000 employees (according to Seamless.AI)

**Alternative Estimate:** ~1,137 employees (according to Growjo.com)

**Key Growth Context:**
- The company doubled its staff in 2021 according to Dallas Innovates reporting
- This growth coincided with their $95M Series B funding round in December 2021
- The company has been in rapid expansion mode since then
- Currently hiring for engineering positions including Senior Software Engineer roles

**Important Distinction:**
ShiftSmart has over 2.2 million workers on their platform across 57 countries, but these are gig workers/contractors who use the platform for flexible work opportunities - they are not full-time employees of ShiftSmart. The actual ShiftSmart corporate employees (the people who work directly for the company building and operating the platform) appear to be in the 500-1,100 range based on the most recent available data.

**Corporate Structure:**
- Headquarters: Dallas, Texas with New York operations
- Global presence supporting operations in 57 countries
- Technology-focused team building and maintaining the platform
- Active recruitment for engineering and technical roles</p><h2></h2><h2>Services and Capabilities</h2><h3>Worker Services</h3><ul><li><p>Customer service roles</p></li><li><p>Merchandising</p></li><li><p>Lead generation</p></li><li><p>Mystery shopping</p></li><li><p>Various hourly positions across industries</p></li></ul><h3>Platform Features</h3><ul><li><p>Intuitive scheduling interface</p></li><li><p>Real-time shift matching</p></li><li><p>Performance tracking and reviews</p></li><li><p>Payment processing and management</p></li><li><p>Quality assurance tools</p></li><li><p>Mobile-first experience</p></li></ul><h2>Market Opportunity and Growth</h2><h3>Market Drivers</h3><ul><li><p>Fundamental shift in labor market dynamics</p></li><li><p>Increased demand for flexible work arrangements</p></li><li><p>Digital transformation of workforce management</p></li><li><p>Post-COVID acceleration of on-demand labor trends</p></li><li><p>Growing need for scalable workforce solutions</p></li></ul><h3>Growth Strategy</h3><ul><li><p>Expansion of worker base and geographic reach</p></li><li><p>Enhancement of platform technology and AI capabilities</p></li><li><p>Deepening relationships with enterprise clients</p></li><li><p>Potential expansion into new industry verticals</p></li><li><p>Continued investment in "People-First" approach</p></li></ul><h2>Investment and Valuation</h2><p>While specific valuation figures are not publicly disclosed, ShiftSmart has attracted significant investment from top-tier venture capital firms, indicating strong investor confidence in the company's growth potential and market position.</p><p>The company appears to be positioning for potential future funding rounds or liquidity events, with pre-IPO investment opportunities available through platforms like Forge Global.</p><h2>Key Challenges and Considerations</h2><h3>Industry Challenges</h3><ul><li><p>Regulatory compliance across multiple jurisdictions</p></li><li><p>Competition from established players and new entrants</p></li><li><p>Economic sensitivity of hourly labor markets</p></li><li><p>Need for continuous technology innovation</p></li><li><p>Balancing worker flexibility with employer needs</p></li></ul><h3>Strategic Focus Areas</h3><ul><li><p>Maintaining quality standards while scaling</p></li><li><p>Technology platform enhancement and automation</p></li><li><p>Geographic expansion and localization</p></li><li><p>Regulatory compliance and worker classification issues</p></li><li><p>Sustainable unit economics and profitability path</p></li></ul><h2>Conclusion</h2><p>ShiftSmart has established itself as a significant player in the workforce management and gig economy space, with strong funding, impressive scale, and notable enterprise clients. The company's focus on technology-driven solutions for the hourly labor market, combined with its "People-First" philosophy, positions it well to capitalize on ongoing trends toward flexible work arrangements.</p><p>The substantial funding raised and continued growth trajectory suggest ShiftSmart is well-positioned to expand its market presence and potentially pursue additional growth opportunities or liquidity events in the future.</p><hr><p><em>Research compiled on September 18, 2025</em><br><em>Sources: Company website, LinkedIn, TechCrunch, CB Insights, Dallas Innovates, HR Tech Feed, and other industry publications</em></p>
